    },
    {
      "id": "claim_457db69200e64922843bec6f22f28243",
      "statement": "During a network partition, CAP requires a distributed system to choose between latest-write consistency and serving every request; asynchronous processing, cache invalidation, and asynchronous replication create eventual-consistency windows in which reads can be stale before convergence.",
